c choice. By flipping D4, I effectively split the opponent's pieces (separating D3 and D5), disrupting their structure. It also establishes a strong diagonal axis (C3-D4-E5) for me, which is a favorable shape in the opening. Additionally, C3 limits the opponent's good responses compared to E3, which would give them multiple strong options on the F-row.\n\nAnswer: (C,3)"}
